WEBVTT

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.950
The intermission between acts is
apparently for the actors, not the audience.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:43.330
It's time for them to prepare their minds
and their bodies for the climax in the second act.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.790
Our summer vacation intermission ended,

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.000
and the new fall semester, leading
to the Ayanagi Festival, has begun!

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.370
"Ayanagi Festival"

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.750
The performance will be on the first day.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.750
The musical department's performances
are all assigned to this day.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.250
Although it's still a test stage,

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.160
the difference between this and the debut
performance is that there is an audience.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.120
The Ayanagi Festival is a
big event the whole school puts on.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.500
Every year, the general public and even people
from the musical world gather in swarms.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.830
We will finally get an audience.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.160
Aw man, I'm getting excited!

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.620
That environment is only
natural for a pro, though.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.410
Oh no, just imagining it makes me dizzy...

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.500
What piece should we perform?

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.370
Let's show the audience something with a
"bang" that will make them go "Ah!" in surprise,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.580
and hit them with a "boom"!

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.830
Hoshitani, that's not concrete at all.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:43.040
It's not just the piece
you have to decide, boys.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.370
You also have to think about publicity
and staging by yourselves.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.290
So our production ability
will also be evaluated, huh?

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.200
There are two main things
you will be evaluated on:

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.450
Your ability to attract an audience
and votes from the general public.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.120
I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:01.370
Well, as long as I'm there, we'll have
no problems getting an audience.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.830
Looks like things will get busy, huh, Nayuki?

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.540
There won't be time to be nervous!

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.410
Hoshitani, you look like you're having
fun even though it's the test stage...

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:14.540
I saw the high schooler
I admire at the Ayanagi Festival,

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.370
so I'm so happy that we'll get
to stand on the same stage as him.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.910
That carefree optimism you're so good at, huh?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.660
It's fine, isn't it? It's just like him.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.330
All right! Let's create a great performance!

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.910
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:44.250
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:51.370
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:59.250
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.750
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:07.290
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:15.540
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:21.790
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.830
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:30.290
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.000
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.790
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:44.450
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.450
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.000
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.500
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.290
"Act 8"

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.290
As usual, there will be three stages.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.950
The first is the Ayanagi Grand Performance Hall.
It is the academy's main hall.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.330
It can fit 1,500 people. That's crazy!

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.410
We couldn't fill that...

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:12.330
Two of the Star Teams will perform there.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.750
Next is Ayanagi Small Hall.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:20.500
It is a compact hall that has 200 seats.
The remaining three Star Teams will perform there.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.200
There's a difference even within the Star Teams?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:30.040
And the five regular teams
will be on a special outdoor stage...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.830
Yuzuriha, if you will.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.870
<i>Oui</i> . Everyone, quiet please.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:39.370
The special stage has the disadvantage
of having limited equipment,

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.950
but it does have the advantage
of having unlimited seating.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:48.000
In the past, there were even cases where
they had a larger audience than the halls.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.870
Don't give up.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:50.790
Seriously?!

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.870
Let's give this a try!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:59.040
Teams who have decided where to
perform should apply with the Kao Council.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.790
If more than one team
applies for the same stage,

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:04.410
they will be assigned in
an impartial and fair way.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.290
You are dismissed.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.160
We want the grand performance hall, right?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.250
A-Are you serious?

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.410
It has the newest equipment
and the best acoustics.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.750
Of course, it also has the best backstage area.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.910
No complaints here.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.750
But it seats 1,500!

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.200
No problem!

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:28.250
You've got the Tengenji successor who
normally performs in front of more than twice that.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:31.660
I just hope that applies
for a high school festival, too.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.410
What did you say?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.870
Which means, publicity will be key, huh?

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:39.410
Wh-What? No one has any reservations?

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.660
You guys are gonna
do something fun again, right?

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.410
Team Otori, I'm looking forward to it!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.120
Could it be...

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.370
...people have high expectations for us?

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.580
Looks like it.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.410
I feel motivated all of a sudden!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.870
Aren't you always motivated?

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.950
Hey, but are we really going
to do the grand performance hall?

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.000
--Yup.
--'Course.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.040
Of course.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:07.910
Ayanagi Grand Performance Hall has
slots open in the morning and afternoon.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.580
Of course, we want to go last.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:11.790
Our voices will be more
warmed up in the afternoon, too.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:15.790
And if we're last, then we can go
around and watch the other teams first.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:19.540
Isn't it unusual for you
two to have the same opinion?

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:25.950
One person has two eyes...
And there will be 1,500 people...

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.950
Nayuki! Are you okay?

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:34.120
Don't worry about me... Just make
it work with the four of you somehow...

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.910
His stage fright's pretty bad.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.500
Let me borrow this for a sec.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.410
Oh, Yuki? Sorry to surprise you.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:43.660
It's Tengenji.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.620
Will you lend me your body sometime?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:46.950
B-Body?

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:49.500
I'm glad you're quick to understand.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.120
I'm counting on you then.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:54.120
I won't let you...

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.870
...lay a finger on my little sister!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:01.200
She said she'd bring that tea
to the Ayanagi Festival, too.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.250
You'll be fine then, right?

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.750
"Tea"

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.750
I'm from Team Otori.
Please accept our application.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.040
Are you serious about this?

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.290
Yes, sir!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.910
I'm from Team Hiragi.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.790
"Team Otori did it!"

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.540
"I heard Hiragi and Otori both applied
for the afternoon grand performance hall slot!"

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:28.790
"Hiragi is more suitable."

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:29.540
"Hiragi is more suitable."
"Morning's fine for them."

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.540
"They won't withdraw?"

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.290
"It's just like them to be reckless. It's great."

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:34.540
"I want to see what kind of performance
they'll put on at the grand performance hall."

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.540
"They'll change history."

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.540
"They'll change history."
"Expecting a lot from Team Otori."

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.540
Akatsuki, sir? Wh-What are you...?

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:44.200
I don't like things like this.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:50.870
Now's your chance to back off.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.330
Who's gonna back off, you boor?!

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:58.950
Okay, everyone. It's time
for your impartial and fair fate!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.700
This is a match to determine who will be
in the last slot for the grand performance hall.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.120
Ready?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.830
Excuse me, will this match use French rules?

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.830
F-French? What's that?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.410
Don't worry. We'll use Japanese rules.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.870
No "well" then.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:15.910
Okay!

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.830
Huh? "Well"?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.200
In France, they have
another option called "well."

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.000
Apparently, this is called " <i>puits</i> ."

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.200
" <i>Puits</i> "?!

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.080
What does that beat--?

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.500
Hoshitani!

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.660
You don't have to worry about it.

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:33.200
<i>Puits</i> .

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.500
Calm down, Hoshitani.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:37.790
<i>Puits</i> ...

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:41.080
And now, we will begin. Rock... paper...

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.290
<i>Puits</i> !

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.120
Huh?

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.000
That's "rock."

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.290
We have a winner!

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.830
Team Hiragi will be in the last slot
for the Ayanagi Grand Performance Hall!

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.000
Yes!

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.620
What a relief.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.660
<i>Puits</i> ... Well...

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.700
He was defeated on a psychological level, huh?

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:07.410
Sorry, Hoshitani! I've never lost
at rock-paper-scissors before!

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.080
If Team Otori becomes
even more positively regarded,

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:19.040
Ayanagi's traditions may also be shaken.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.040
Are you okay with that?

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.950
They have fulfilled the minimum
requirements set by the school,

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.330
and remained candidates
for the musical department.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.200
I have no objections.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.750
You're just saying that!

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:37.160
You are restricted by
your respect for the rules.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.950
Otori's existence jeopardizes
the school's traditions.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:42.370
You know that, right?

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.410
Excuse me.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.120
You are supporting him too much!

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:53.750
I know. If you won't make a move...

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.080
...then I will.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:02.290
So even though we couldn't get the last slot,
we successfully got the grand performance hall!

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:06.750
The other three teams asked
for Ayanagi Small Hall, huh?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.040
Because using the same space
makes it easier to be compared.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.870
They went with the safe route, huh?

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:14.040
How unmanly.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.750
Well, thanks to that, we got what we wanted.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.830
Next is the performance piece.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:24.120
I'm looking forward to seeing
what you'll choose, boys.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.200
Yes, sir!

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:30.540
Oh, you have to apply for funds, too,
so make sure you decide by next week.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.870
All right! Let's decide quickly!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.660
Today is hot, too, isn't it?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.790
It's the lingering summer heat.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.160
I heard you did a combined
training camp with Hiragi?

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.370
It was a coincidence.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:59.040
You're lucky you're related
and can use the same villa.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.160
Will this take a while?

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.000
I'll treat you to something.
Wanna go get some tea?

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.580
I don't want any!

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.080
Oh, really?

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.700
Stop tormenting Hiragi so much!

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:14.950
He's different from you!

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:22.750
He is responsible for Ayanagi Academy
and upholding its traditions!

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:27.160
What are you to him?

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:34.410
In order to move people emotionally,
I think it needs to be easy to understand.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.250
It would probably be best to use a famous work.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.700
Like <i>Les Mis</i> or <i>The Wizard of Oz</i> ?

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:42.660
We can't do a major work
like that with the five of us.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.040
We can just do parts of it.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.660
The grand performance hall equipment
should be enough to make it look good.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:51.040
Relying on equipment is
something an amateur would do.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.870
We need to show them our acting first.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.500
I know that.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.040
Now, now. Let's keep thinking about it.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.080
Publicity will be key, right?

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.580
We can't start unless we can gather an audience.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:08.000
The play I went to watch with my sisters
the other day had a really cool poster, too!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.500
It's also important to have
copy that will draw people in.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.450
What, you got tickets?

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.500
Yuki and Tsumugi called using the house phone

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.250
and their cellphones at the same time.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.700
Lucky, I want to go watch it at least once.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:21.410
You guys.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:22.700
Let's go together next time.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.580
Yay!

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.580
Right now, we're deciding our piece!

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.120
I'm heading out first.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.700
It's really hard to decide, huh?

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:36.830
It's because <i>someone</i> was going off topic.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.450
I'm worried about the future.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.040
Wanna go look at the
grand performance hall sometime?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.700
Don't change the subject again!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.250
What did you want to talk about?

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:54.450
I was surprised that your team
wanted a grand performance hall slot.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:57.120
They lost at rock-paper-scissors, though.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.870
Why didn't you have them use Ayanagi Small Hall?

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:05.450
It would be best not to be more conspicuous
in a bad way than you already are.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.870
We only got it because
no other teams asked for it.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:12.040
If you have any objections,
you should tell Akatsuki and the others.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.580
Why did we turn out like this?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.620
I wonder...

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.290
It's huge!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.540
I can't believe these are
school facilities. It's impressive.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.080
Oh? You've never been here before, Kuga?

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.830
Remember, he was late
to the entrance ceremony...

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.160
Doesn't bother me.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.950
Come on, let's go.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.830
We're performing in such a big hall...?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:58.750
It's breathtaking seeing it from the stage.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.700
That feels great!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.040
We can really perform here!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.580
I'm so excited!

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:25.870
Do you have a minute?

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.750
It has been bothering me, as well.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:34.620
But if it's something Hiragi decided...

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:37.200
Is it really okay to leave it to Hiragi?

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.660
What do you mean?

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:42.370
If people become used to
accepting those who aren't as good,

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:44.830
then the Ayanagi brand will be tainted.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:48.200
If everyone on the Kao Council is equal,

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.870
then I thought we had
some responsibility, as well.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.750
Tengenji, what was the idea you had?

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:58.040
Put the team's strength out front.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:58.950
Strength?

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:00.580
In other words, me.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:05.250
If we make the famous <i>kabuki</i> plays
<i>Kanjincho</i> and <i>Dojoji</i> into musicals--

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.750
Of course, you will be
writing the script, right?

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.750
No way. We should leave it
to Kuga, who can play piano--

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:14.870
I can play piano, but I can't write a script.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.450
I <i>can</i> draw, though.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.790
I know! What about this?

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:22.540
There are musicals that bring cars
and helicopters into big theaters, right?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:26.540
Kuga could wear a motorcycle jacket
and show up on a motorcycle!

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:30.200
And then he could defeat a bunch of monsters--

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:33.910
What's the point of doing a
stunt show in the grand performance hall?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.620
I guess it kind of turned into one...

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.500
What if we did something major?
Like <i>Romeo and Juliet</i> or something?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:44.450
We could have the young noble of the <i>kabuki</i>
world who can play female parts play Juliet.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:46.160
What?!

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:51.160
Hey! Why the heck are you called Romeo?

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:54.790
Hurry up and give up
your family name, you boor!

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:56.790
Nope. Nope. Nope.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.540
I'd refuse before you could ask!

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.290
The stunt show would be better...

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.370
Not that, either.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:03.700
We should do <i>kabuki</i> , after all--

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:05.540
But who would write the script?

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:09.870
Something we can do with five people
that can attract an audience...

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.410
Is there anything like that?

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:19.660
What we have a problem with is that
Otori's actions degrade the Kao Council,

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.410
and consequently, Ayanagi Academy.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:27.330
It's true that the way he
does things is unpardonable.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.580
Do you agree with them, Yuzuriha?

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:35.620
I love Otori. But I love the
school just about as much, so...

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:40.000
Right now, the members of Team Otori

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:44.000
are starting to be treated by
the students as revolutionaries.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.700
If we let things continue like this,

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.870
we won't be able to protect
the traditions of Ayanagi Academy.

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:51.830
Then, what do you want me to do?

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:54.540
If Otori leaves the Kao Council,

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.950
then they would inevitably
lose their status as a Star Team.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:02.040
When Team Otori gets demoted to
a regular team, they will fall into disorder.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:06.040
They'll also be certain to fail
the test stage at the Ayanagi Festival.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:10.080
Once that happens, the strange enthusiasm
people have for them will also die down.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:11.330
Hiragi.

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:14.250
Let's protect the traditions of Ayanagi!

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:19.450
Let me have some time to think this over.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:39.330
"Theater Journal"

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.200
We can't come to a decision...

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:31.790
There's not even a hint of
our opinions coming together...

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.540
Get a hold of yourselves, everyone!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.120
We're running out of time!

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:38.500
What, are you doing penance or something?

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:42.290
Weren't you talking about musicals, boys?

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:45.870
The expressions you have aren't like Team Otori.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:49.040
Like us...

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:52.660
Space junk of the Star Teams...
It's like we're stardust...

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:54.080
That's pretty good!

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:56.450
The five of us are a team.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.120
We can do it.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.080
Let's have fun with this stardust rebellion!

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:06.250
We should put on the best
performance we can in our own way!

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:11.620
I see... I forgot about
having fun without noticing...

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:36.620
♪ My heart's beating faster ♪

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:39.620
♪ I'm getting excited ♪

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:45.200
♪ All right! Everything will
turn out all right somehow ♪

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.910
♪ Sometimes we're wrong ♪

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.540
♪ Sometimes we go out of bounds ♪

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.450
♪ Everything is correct ♪

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:56.120
♪ Everything sparkles ♪

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:58.620
♪ Let's try doing things we're
good at and <i>not</i> good at! (Yeah!) ♪

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.000
♪ Everyone's different,
but that's good, too (Good!) ♪

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.580
♪ It'll slowly get more fun (Yeah!) ♪

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:09.540
♪ We can make what we imagine happen ♪

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.000
♪ What about our dream?! ♪

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.370
♪ Is it over there?! ♪

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:18.370
♪ Bursting out and shining the way we want ♪

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.910
♪ Doing things our way ♪

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:23.700
♪ We're not alone, let's become one ♪

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:28.410
♪ Even if we're small, gather close ♪

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:32.080
♪ We'll show you a dream
you've never seen before ♪

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.000
♪ (Are you OK?) ♪

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.950
♪ (Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!) ♪

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:39.000
♪ (Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!) ♪

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.290
♪ (Dream go!) ♪

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.540
We should do a <i>revue</i> that focuses on dancing.

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:58.000
It'll be called, "Stardust Musical"!

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.500
We're...

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.410
...Stardust!

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:06.410
Looks like you can have
fun playing with that, boys.

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.080
"Breaking news! Team Otori
decided on their piece!"

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.830
Seriously?

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.830
Morning! You're going to do
a <i>revue</i> in the grand performance hall?

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.370
What kind?

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.200
You'll have to wait and see!

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:19.120
The Team Otori phenomenon is amazing.

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:21.950
Hah, they're just trick stars.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:24.700
You look happy, Tatsumi.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:29.830
We can aim higher when
we have charismatic rivals.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:39.250
Kuga's been saying that he
wanted to work on the publicity poster.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.660
Let's think of a good quote to put on it!

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:44.040
I'll go turn in the
application for the equipment.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.120
Thanks!

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:47.700
I'm done.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:52.580
What is this?

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.500
"Stardust Musical."

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.200
Um, what part of it is stardust?

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:58.660
Can't you tell by looking?

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:01.000
"Team Otori"

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:01.000
It's very original...

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:18.790
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:25.330
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:28.830
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:33.120
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:33.120 --> 00:22:37.250
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:40.500
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:44.080
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:48.040
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:51.200
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:55.080
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:58.580
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:02.330
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:05.870
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:09.580
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:15.580
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:33.410
Don't you feel it, too, Hiragi?

00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:35.750
This strange atmosphere.

00:23:35.750 --> 00:23:39.290
Is it really all right to continue
tolerating what Otori is doing?

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:45.120
I think it's time to make a decision,

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:48.700
as someone who protects
the future of Ayanagi Academy.

00:23:50.750 --> 00:23:52.200
Very well.

00:23:54.870 --> 00:24:19.200
"Act 9"

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:57.910
Yuzuriha, try saying " <i>croissant</i> ."

00:23:57.910 --> 00:23:58.950
<i>Croissant</i> .

00:23:58.950 --> 00:23:59.950
<i>Mont Saint-Michel</i> .

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:01.250
<i>Mont Saint-Michel</i> .

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:02.080
<i>Triumphal arch</i> .

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:03.750
<i>Triumphal arch</i> !

00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:06.330
Did you really used to live in France?

00:24:06.330 --> 00:24:09.120
<i>Oui</i> ? <i>Oui</i> , <i>oui</i> . <i>Oui</i> !

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:19.200
"shiny"
"Please watch again♪ Oh, Toraishi!"
